      "turn": 0,
      "assistant": "I'll analyze the input-output pair first.\n\n**Observation:** Input is 10\u00d78, output is 5\u00d74. The input splits into a 2\u00d72 arrangement of 5\u00d74 tiles:\n- Top-left: all 9s\n- Top-right: 6s with two 4s\n- Bottom-left: 6s with two 4s (identical to top-right)\n- Bottom-right: all 9s\n\nThe output equals the top-right tile (= bottom-left tile), i.e. the tile containing the 4s.\n\nLet me propose candidate rules.",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_01a0c81f41a47421a47c0ed5",
          "name": "propose_hypotheses",
          "arguments": "{\"hypotheses\":[{\"nl\":\"Split into 2x2 blocks of 5x4; output the first block (reading order) containing the color 4.\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    blocks=[]\\n    for i in range(2):\\n        for j in range(2):\\n            blocks.append([row[j*bc:(j+1)*bc] for row in grid[i*br:(i+1)*br]])\\n    for b in blocks:\\n        if any(4 in row for row in b):\\n            return b\\n    return blocks[0]\"},{\"nl\":\"Output the top-right 5x4 quadrant block.\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    return [row[bc:] for row in grid[:br]]\"},{\"nl\":\"Split into 2x2 blocks; output the block with the fewest 9s (first in reading order on ties).\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    blocks=[]\\n    for i in range(2):\\n        for j in range(2):\\n            blocks.append([row[j*bc:(j+1)*bc] for row in grid[i*br:(i+1)*br]])\\n    return min(blocks, key=lambda b: sum(r.count(9) for r in b))\"},{\"nl\":\"Split into 2x2 blocks; output the first block (reading order) that is not monochrome.\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    blocks=[]\\n    for i in range(2):\\n        for j in range(2):\\n            blocks.append([row[j*bc:(j+1)*bc] for row in grid[i*br:(i+1)*br]])\\n    for b in blocks:\\n        vals=set(v for r in b for v in r)\\n        if len(vals)>1:\\n            return b\\n    return blocks[0]\"},{\"nl\":\"Output the bottom-left 5x4 quadrant block.\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    return [row[:bc] for row in grid[br:]]\"},{\"nl\":\"Split into 2x2 blocks; output the block with the most 6s (first in reading order on ties).\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    blocks=[]\\n    for i in range(2):\\n        for j in range(2):\\n            blocks.append([row[j*bc:(j+1)*bc] for row in grid[i*br:(i+1)*br]])\\n    return max(blocks, key=lambda b: sum(r.count(6) for r in b))\"},{\"nl\":\"Split into 2x2 blocks; output the first block (reading order) that is not all 9s.\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    blocks=[]\\n    for i in range(2):\\n        for j in range(2):\\n            blocks.append([row[j*bc:(j+1)*bc] for row in grid[i*br:(i+1)*br]])\\n    for b in blocks:\\n        if any(v!=9 for r in b for v in r):\\n            return b\\n    return blocks[0]\"},{\"nl\":\"Split into 2x2 blocks; output the block containing the most 4s.\",\"code\":\"def transform(grid):\\n    R=len(grid); C=len(grid[0])\\n    br=R//2; bc=C//2\\n    blocks=[]\\n    for i in range(2):\\n        for j in range(2):\\n            blocks.append([row[j*bc:(j+1)*bc] for row in grid[i*br:(i+1)*br]])\\n    cands=[b for b in blocks if any(4 in row for row in b)]\\n    if not cands:\\n        return blocks[0]\\n    return max(cands, key=lambda b: sum(r.count(4) for r in b))\"}]}"
